|~ `::proj`, the step that reads a part of a value, and the refusals of
   a read that misses. ~|

::proj
  |~~ The step of a projection, `/a/0/b`: it reads a part of the value in
      the pipe by keys and indices, a negative index from the end, and a
      miss answers an error, never null, so a misspelled field is found
      where it is read. `/` is the value itself. A key is written as a
      keyword is, bare, in quotes, `/"foo bar"`, or with its colon when it
      is a path, `/:qlang/error`, which is one key where `/qlang/error`
      is two. As a record, `:path` is the keys and indices it walks,
      `[]` for `/`.
      ::snippet~({:a {:b [5 6]}} | /a/b/-1) answers `6`.
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :pipeline)

      ~(~(/items/0/name) | first | /path | eq [:items 0 :name])
      ~(~(/) | first | /path | eq [])
      ~({:"foo bar" {:qlang/error 1}} | /"foo bar"/:qlang/error | eq 1)
      ~({:qlang {:error 2}} | /qlang/error | eq 2)
      ~(5 | mul / | eq 25)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/proj}

::ProjPayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A ::proj payload is a Map of `:path` a Vec of keys and
      integers.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        ::proj{:path "items"}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::ProjPayloadNotSchemaError :path]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The ::proj prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      key that reads as an index is written as the index.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        ::proj{:path [:"0"]}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::ProjReadBackDiffersError "/\"0\""]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjectionFieldNotOnValueClassError
  |~~ Projection segment names no declaration of the signature it
      reads.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        ::vec/join | spec | /missing
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::ProjectionFieldNotOnValueClassError "missing"]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjectionIndexOutOfBoundsError
  |~~ Projection `/n` — the integer index resolves outside
      the Vec or Set subject's `[0, length)` range.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        [10 20 30] | /99
        !| [type /index /length]
        |  eq [::ProjectionIndexOutOfBoundsError 99 3]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjectionKeyNotInMapError
  |~~ Projection `/key` — the named key is absent from the
      Map subject (strict-miss). Use `at :key` for
      null-coalescing access.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        {:a 1} | /b
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::ProjectionKeyNotInMapError "b"]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjectionSubjectNotProjectableError
  |~~ Projection `/key` requires a map, a vector, a set or a tagged
      value as its subject; null and other shapes lift to this error.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        42 | /foo
        !| [type /key /actualType]
        |  eq [::ProjectionSubjectNotProjectableError "foo" ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::ProjectionSequenceKeyNotIntegerError
  |~~ Projection segment is a non-numeric string but the
      subject is a Vec or Set — sequence indices must be integer
      offsets, a set's in its one order.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        [10 20 30] | /name
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::ProjectionSequenceKeyNotIntegerError "name"]
       )
       ~(
        #[:a :b :c] | /name
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::ProjectionSequenceKeyNotIntegerError "name"]
       )
  ~~|
